 r←secret MaskQueryString text;CR;LF;eol;q;e;query;pairs;b
⍝ `text` is a request target such as '/path?a=1&b=2', a request line such as 'GET /path?a=1 HTTP/1.1',
⍝ or raw HTTP data that starts with a request line.
⍝ Returns `text` with the value of every query parameter whose name is in `secret` (upper case, see
⍝ `SecretQueryParms`) replaced by "***". Only the first line is looked at: that is where the query is.
⍝ Names are compared as they are, so an encoded name such as 'to%6Ben' is not recognized.
 (CR LF)←⎕UCS 13 10
 r←text
 eol←⌊/text⍳CR LF                                    ⍝ End of the first line
 q←text⍳'?'
 :If q≥eol
     :Return
 :EndIf
 e←q+¯1+⌊/(q↓text)⍳' ',CR,LF                        ⍝ The query ends with the first blank or the line
 query←q↓e↑text
 pairs←'&'{1↓¨(⍺=⍵)⊂⍵}'&',query
 b←{'='∊⍵}¨pairs
 b[⍸b]←(1 ⎕C{(¯1+⍵⍳'=')↑⍵}¨b/pairs)∊secret
 pairs[⍸b]←{(⍵↑⍨⍵⍳'='),'***'}¨b/pairs
 r←(q↑text),(1↓∊'&',¨pairs),e↓text
